hash(string) -> {result: Crypto.hash(string), length: Crypto.calculateLength(string)}

Crypto.calculateLength returns a number. It returns a number that is calculated based on the length of the string.
The above two functions returns a number. It is the length of the string, in characters, minus one. (That is, length of the string minus 1)
That being said, you can also pass in a function that returns a string. (Which will do something like the stringify function)
